{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsDerived","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsDerived","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.OcneanuWeightMarkov3"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonicalInstance_eq_ocneanuWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonicalInstance_eq_ocneanuWeight","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsDerived.lean#L101-L112","doc":"**The instance is the `n = 3` slice of the general-`n` Ocneanu weight at `z_D`**, on all three\npartitions of `3`.  Chained through `OcneanuWeightMarkov3`, which needs `q² ≠ 1` for its hook\ndenominators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonicalInstance_eq_markovWeights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonicalInstance_eq_markovWeights","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsDerived.lean#L90-L99","doc":"**The default instance resolves to the derived weights**, field by field.  The left sides\nelaborate through instance resolution; the right sides are `HeckeMarkov3`'s solved weights at\n`z_D`.  Block order: `y3 ↔ (3) ↔ markovWeight0`, `y21 ↔ (2,1) ↔ markovWeight2`,\n`y111 ↔ (1³) ↔ markovWeight1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovWeight1_at_markovZD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovWeight1_at_markovZD","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsDerived.lean#L80-L88","doc":"**`y₍₁³₎ = 0` is the derived sign-block weight at `z_D`.**  The vanishing is not imposed:\n`markovWeight1` carries the factor `z(q²+1) − q³`, which is zero exactly at `z_D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_y21_eq_markovWeight2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_y21_eq_markovWeight2","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsDerived.lean#L70-L78","doc":"**`y₍₂,₁₎` is the derived two-dimensional-block weight.**\n`canonical_y21 q = markovWeight2 q z_D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_y3_eq_markovWeight0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_y3_eq_markovWeight0","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsDerived.lean#L61-L68","doc":"**`y₍₃₎` is the derived trivial-block weight.**  `canonical_y3 q = markovWeight0 q z_D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsDerived.lean#L58-L59","doc":"Convention D's Markov parameter, `z_D = q³/(q²+1)`, as a named function of `q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}